  "extraction_notes": "Report date is printed 'June 25th, 2025' although it covers January 1 - December 31, 2025 and cites 2026 samples (presumably a typo for 2026). The system splits results by Source water (raw well water), Treated water (delivered) and customer plumbing; source_group records which. Source-water iron (700 ppb), manganese (545 ppb) and turbidity (11.65 NTU) exceed secondary MCLs, but the report states these are removed by the treatment plant and that no MCL or other standard was violated - so they are not listed as violations. Sample dates are printed as year ranges ('2024-2026'); sample_year records the last year of the range. Several rows carry apparent unit errors (lead/copper in 'ppt', fluoride and nitrate in 'ppb', barium '(ppm)') that were copied as printed and flagged in notes. Table 6b LEAD row shows spreadsheet errors ('#N/A', '#DIV/0!'). Page numbers are the PDF's 1-based pages (14 total)."
